    "title": "Hal Turner Radio Show - China's Supreme Court first ruling under \"anti-foreign sanctions\" law",
    "text": "A Shanghai court ordered a Singaporean company to pay over 4.9 million yuan for refusing to deliver goods due to US sanctions.\nThe Supreme People's Court says this judgment was the first to \"explicitly establish the mandatory application\" of the five year old law. Chinese law FORBIDS anyone from honoring \"Sanctions\" imposed by any foreign government. The law is aimed specifically at the United States, but also applies to other foreign countries.\nThe court held that the Singaporean company \"could not use a foreign country's discriminatory restrictions\" as a defense under Article 12 of China's \"anti-Foreign Sanctions\" law.",
    "summary": "A Shanghai court ordered a Singaporean company to pay over 4.9 million yuan for refusing to deliver goods due to US sanctions. The Supreme People's Court says this judgment was the first to \"explicitly establish the mandatory application\" of the five year old law. Chinese law FORBIDS anyone from honoring \"Sanctions\" imposed by any foreign government. The law is aimed specifically at the United States, but also applies to other foreign countries. The court held that the Singaporean company \"could not use a foreign country's discriminatory restrictions\" as a defense under Article 12 of China's \"anti-Foreign Sanctions\" law.",
